Nim 2.2.10 — Lunar-style modernization trial v6

Root cause fixed:
- Nim 2.2.x expects the global configuration at /etc/nim/nim.cfg.
- The old Lunar BUILD installed config/nim*.cfg directly into /etc.
- During `koch boot`, the first iteration uses the installed Nim compiler.
  Without the global nim.cfg, stdlib search paths such as $lib/pure are missing,
  causing failures such as:
      dist/checksums/src/checksums/sha1.nim Error: cannot open file: strutils

Changes:
1. Install config/nim*.cfg under /etc/nim/.
2. Treat an installed Nim as reusable only if all of these exist:
      /usr/bin/nim
      /usr/lib/nim/lib/system.nim
      /etc/nim/nim.cfg
3. If the config is absent (as on the current migrated installation),
   PRE_BUILD unpacks csources_v3 and BUILD performs one clean C bootstrap.

DETAILS remains unchanged from v5. There is no DEPENDS file.
